{
  "_comment": [
    "WHICH LAYERS MEAN THE SAME THING IN EACH APP, so the layers a reader has on",
    "travel with them when they move from one state's app to another (a click or",
    "a search outside the state, the state menu, the footer row). Asked for by the",
    "operator on 2026-10-13: \"attempt to maintain the currently toggled layers",
    "when moving from one state to another.\"",
    "",
    "One row per concept; under it, each app's tag and the layer id (or ids) that",
    "answer that concept there. Ids differ between apps for one thing (Illinois's",
    "`congress` is Iowa's `us-house`), and ONE ID CAN MEAN TWO THINGS, which is why",
    "matching ids alone is not enough: Illinois's `ward` is a city council ward and",
    "Wisconsin's `ward` is an election ward, so Illinois's sits under city-council",
    "and Wisconsin's under voting-precinct. A layer may sit under two concepts",
    "(San Francisco's supervisors are its city council AND its county board), and",
    "an app may answer one concept with two layers (Illinois draws precincts in",
    "Chicago and in the suburban counties as separate layers; each hides where the",
    "other answers). A layer in no row is simply not carried.",
    "",
    "scripts/generate_metro_files.py slices this into each app as LAYER_CONCEPTS",
    "(concept -> that app's ids) and FAILS on a row naming a layer the app does not",
    "register, a row only one app has, or a layer id two LIVE apps both register",
    "that no row carries. A new state adds its column to every row it can answer;",
    "a new layer adds itself to a row when a sibling has the same thing.",
    "",
    "HOW EACH CONCEPT IS DRAWN is the second table, `colors`, so a layer looks the",
    "same in every app. Asked for by the operator on 2026-10-13, the same day: \"Now",
    "that layers are linked across states, i'd like them to be unified on layer",
    "colors.\" Each concept has one line colour and one fill colour, and every layer",
    "under it draws in them in every app; a layer under two concepts takes the",
    "colours of the first of them in this file (San Francisco's supervisors draw as",
    "a county board, New York's cities and towns as a county subdivision).",
    "generate_metro_files.py FAILS on a concept with no colours, on two concepts",
    "sharing one line colour, and on an app whose layer definition carries any other",
    "`color:`, `fillColor:` or `fill:` literal, so a new state takes the colours",
    "when it adds its column and cannot drift from them afterwards. Every line",
    "colour reads at 4.5:1 or better as the small coloured label on a white card,",
    "and scripts/build_dark_map_palette.py derives its dark counterpart from the",
    "whole fleet's colours at once, so one light colour has one dark colour",
    "everywhere.",
    "",
    "HOW WIDE EACH CONCEPT'S LINE IS is the third table, `lines`, asked for by the",
    "operator on 2026-10-13 in the same change as the colours: \"Include the line",
    "style standardization in this change.\" Each concept has one line width",
    "(`weight`, in pixels), and every layer under it draws with it in every app:",
    "the width most apps already used for that kind of layer, Illinois's where two",
    "were used equally often, and the wider where Illinois has no such layer (the",
    "community college districts). NO LAYER'S OWN OUTLINE IS DASHED, in any app, on the",
    "operator's rule of the same day: \"The solid lines are for the district the",
    "selected point falls under. The dashed lines are only for the comparison",
    "tool.\" A dash on the map means a district that crosses the edge of the one",
    "pinned for comparison, so a layer drawn dashed would say that where it is not",
    "true. A concept whose layers are map pins in most apps (stations, post offices,",
    "libraries, schools, early voting) has a null width and keeps each app's own:",
    "Illinois draws schools as building outlines painted by school type, which one",
    "width could not describe. A layer in no concept keeps its own width.",
    "generate_metro_files.py FAILS on a concept with no entry, on a concept layer",
    "carrying any other `weight:` value, and on any `dashArray:` other than null",
    "in an app's own code.",
    "",
    "Concept names appear only in the hand-off link's `carry=` and are never",
    "shared, so unlike layer-codes.json nothing here is permanent."
  ],
